---
import BlogPost from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

// Calories match each item's page on this site.
const treats = [
  { name: 'Kids’ vanilla cone', href: '/items/vanilla-soft-serve-cone', cal: '160' },
  { name: 'DQ Sandwich', href: '/items/dq-sandwich', cal: '~180' },
  { name: 'Dilly Bar', href: '/items/dilly-bar', cal: '~220' },
  { name: 'Non-Dairy Dilly Bar', href: '/items/non-dairy-dilly-bar', cal: '220' },
  { name: 'Small strawberry sundae', href: '/items/strawberry-sundae', cal: '240' },
  { name: 'Small hot fudge sundae', href: '/items/hot-fudge-sundae', cal: '300' },
  { name: 'Mini Oreo Blizzard', href: '/items/oreo-blizzard', cal: '330' },
];
const meals = [
  { name: 'Side salad (no dressing)', href: '/items/side-salad', cal: '20' },
  { name: 'Regular fries', href: '/items/regular-fries', cal: '280' },
  { name: 'Original Cheeseburger', href: '/items/original-cheeseburger', cal: '370' },
  { name: 'Grilled chicken sandwich', href: '/items/grilled-chicken-sandwich', cal: '390' },
  { name: 'Cheese curds (regular)', href: '/items/cheese-curds', cal: '500' },
  { name: 'Double FlameThrower Stackburger', href: '/items/flamethrower-stackburger', cal: '720' },
  { name: '4-piece Chicken Strip Basket', href: '/items/chicken-strip-basket-4pc', cal: '1,020' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is the lowest-calorie item at Dairy Queen?', a: 'A side salad without dressing (about 20 calories) is the lightest food item. For dessert, a Kids’ vanilla cone (about 160 calories) or a DQ Sandwich (about 180 calories) are the lightest treats.' },
  { q: 'What is the healthiest thing to eat at Dairy Queen?', a: 'The grilled chicken sandwich (about 390 calories) with a side salad is one of the most balanced meals. For dessert, choose a Kids’ cone or a Mini Blizzard instead of a larger size.' },
  { q: 'How many calories are in a Blizzard?', a: 'Most Blizzards have about 330–450 calories as a Mini, 560–750 as a Small, 720–1,040 as a Medium and 940–1,370 as a Large, depending on the flavor.' },
  { q: 'Where can I find official Dairy Queen nutrition information?', a: 'Dairy Queen publishes nutrition and allergen details on its website and in the DQ app. Our calorie and nutrition figures come from DQ’s official U.S. nutrition information (current as of August 26, 2024), while our prices are typical estimates that vary by location.' },
];
---
<BlogPost
  title="Dairy Queen Calories & Nutrition Guide (2026)"
  description="Dairy Queen calories at a glance: the lightest treats and meals, Blizzard calories by size, and simple swaps to eat lighter at DQ."
  h1="Dairy Queen Calories and Nutrition: Lighter Choices at DQ"
  crumb="DQ Calories Guide"
  eyebrow="Calories and nutrition"
  image="/Images/dilly-bar.webp"
  imageAlt="Dairy Queen Dilly Bar on a stick"
  datePublished="2026-04-20"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p class="lead"><strong>The lightest treats at Dairy Queen are a Kids’ vanilla cone (about 160 calories), a DQ Sandwich (about 180) and a Dilly Bar (about 220).</strong> For a meal, an Original Cheeseburger (about 370 calories) or a grilled chicken sandwich (about 390) are the lighter choices. The biggest calorie jump at DQ comes from size: a Large Blizzard can have three times the calories of a Mini.</p>

  <p>This guide is for comparing options. It is not medical advice. Calorie and nutrition figures come from Dairy Queen’s official U.S. nutrition information (current as of August 26, 2024); prices are typical estimates that vary by location.</p>

  <h2 id="treats">Lowest-calorie DQ treats</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Treat</th><th>Calories</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{treats.map((t) => <tr><td><a href={t.href}>{t.name}</a></td><td>{t.cal}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Treats on a stick or in a wrapper, like the Dilly Bar and DQ Sandwich, are easy to keep in check because the portion is fixed.</p>

  <h2 id="blizzards">Blizzard calories by size</h2>
  <p>Size matters more than flavor. A Mini <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo Blizzard</a> is about 330 calories, a Small 600, a Medium 820 and a Large 1,050. Richer flavors like <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese’s</a> and <a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard">Cookie Dough</a> run higher. If you want a Blizzard but are watching calories, order a Mini. Full numbers for every flavor are on the <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard menu</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="meals">Calories in DQ food</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Calories</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{meals.map((m) => <tr><td><a href={m.href}>{m.name}</a></td><td>{m.cal}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="swaps">Easy swaps to eat lighter</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mini instead of Small</strong> on any Blizzard saves roughly 200–320 calories.</li>
    <li><strong>Side salad instead of fries</strong> saves about 260 calories (before dressing).</li>
    <li><strong>Double instead of triple</strong> on a burger. The Double FlameThrower is about 720 calories; the Triple is about 910.</li>
    <li><strong>Grilled instead of crispy</strong> chicken sandwich.</li>
    <li><strong>Strawberry or a cone instead of a shake.</strong> A small <a href="/items/chocolate-shake">chocolate shake</a> is about 530 calories.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="drinks">Drinks</h2>
  <p>A small <a href="/items/misty-slush">Misty Slush</a> is about 200 calories and has no fat. Shakes and <a href="/items/moolatte">MooLattés</a> are much heavier, from about 450 calories for a small. See the <a href="/categories/drinks">drinks menu</a> for every size.</p>

  <h2 id="allergies">Food allergies</h2>
  <p>If you are avoiding gluten, nuts or dairy, read our <a href="/blog/dq-gluten-free-allergen-guide">Dairy Queen allergen guide</a> before you order.</p>
</BlogPost>
